attaching and mounting an ebs volume to and ec2 instance : 
1) AWS->EC2->EBS->Volumes
Create volume
vol type,size and AZ (same as EC2)

2) Attaching Volume
click on the volume
actions -> attach volume
select instance, device name (/dev/xvdf)

3) Connecting to EC2 instance
ssh -i key.pem ec2-user@<public_ip>

4) Verify attached disk
lsblk 
/dev/xvda
/dev/xvdf

5) Create a partition
fdisk /dev/xvdf
inside click n,p, enter,enter,enter,w
partprobe

6) Verify new partition
lsblk -fs

7) Format the partition
mkfs.xfs /dev/xvdf1
verify: lsblk -fs

8) Create mount directory
mkdir /mnt/rishit

9) Mount the volume
mount /dev/xvdf1 /mnt/rishit

10) Check persistence of the mount
check uuid of the volume -> blkid /dev/xvdf1
edit fstab -> nano etc/fstab
uuid=<uuid_value> /mnt/rishit xfs defaults.nofail 0 0
save and exit

test: mount -a

11) Verify perisitence
reboot the instance and reconnect to check (df -h)

12) detach and reattach the volume
ec2->volume->actions->detach volume
attach->log in to new instance->create mount directory->mount volume

